#. Scene: Townspeople.
#. Context: Background characters around the city. Most lines change as the story moves on, so one
#. character can have several lines in a row. The script does not record where each character stands;
#. the lines themselves name places (Yarai Ward and Yarai Ginza, Chinatown, Hibarigaoka, Asahi Ward,
#. Seaside Park and the library, the police station, Kitayama University, Mt. Kasagi, Chuo Ward, Toa
#. TV). In 28-43 and 65-78, people who know the player address him by name; several of these change
#. with the occupation chosen at sign-up. 145, 148, 150 are debug placeholders.
#. Speaker: 女性 = Woman (English names as used in the patch).
#. Limit: Text box: 3 lines of 40 letters (20 tiles, 2 letters per tile). The build re-wraps lines, so
#. line breaks are only hints. If a line needs more room, add [wait][box] to start another box.
#. Tags: [wait] = wait for the player to press a button.
#: MESFILE.EVE:0
msgctxt "MESFILE.EVE#0"
msgid ""
"女性：ルンルンルン。\n"
"モーロックのコンサート予約が取れたのよ！\n"
"さっそくチケットガイドで交換しなきゃ。[wait]"
msgstr ""

